%% Styles: a class defined after its point applies (Q15), a point's own style wins over its class
%% (Q16), a class defined twice takes the second (Q17), a class with no definition has no style
%% (Q14), a radius of 0 is kept (Q20), and `color` without `#` is written as given (Q22).
quadrantChart
  title Classes and point styles
  x-axis Low --> High
  y-axis Low --> High
  quadrant-1 A
  quadrant-2 B
  quadrant-3 C
  quadrant-4 D
  Late class:::late: [0.2, 0.8]
  Own wins:::first: [0.4, 0.8] color: #00ff00
  Zero radius:::first: [0.6, 0.8] radius: 0
  Undefined class:::nothing: [0.8, 0.8]
  Without hash:::first: [0.3, 0.3] color: abcdef
  Short hex:::first: [0.5, 0.3] color: #abc, stroke-color: #123
  Stroke only:::late: [0.7, 0.3] stroke-width: 4px
  classDef first color: #ff0000, radius: 8
  classDef first color: #0000ff, stroke-color: #00ff00
  classDef late radius: 12, stroke-width: 2px, stroke-color: #101010
